IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vic-nouns`
IMPORT `vic-interpretation-time`

-- Part IV -- Provisions applicable to Acts and subordinate instruments.
-- This module: ss 35 to 37 (aids to interpretation, what forms part of an Act, gender and number), ss 38AAA, 38AA, 38EA(2),
-- ss 38M to 38P (publication of notices) and ss 39 to 39B.
-- The definitions of s 38 and the sections that continue it are in vic-definitions.l4; s 44 (time) is in vic-interpretation-time.l4.

§ `Part IV -- Provisions applicable to Acts and subordinate instruments`

§§ `s 35 Principles of and aids to interpretation`

-- s 35(a): a construction that would promote the purpose or object underlying the Act or subordinate instrument (whether or not expressly stated) is preferred to a construction that would not.
-- src:479 | (a) a construction that would promote the purpose or object underlying the Act or subordinate instrument (whether or not that purpose or object is expressly stated in the Act or subordinate instrument) shall be preferred to a construction that would not promote that purpose or object; and
@ref s 35(a) (src:479)
GIVEN firstConstructionWouldPromoteThePurposeOrObject IS A BOOLEAN, secondConstructionWouldPromoteThePurposeOrObject IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s35(a) the first construction is preferred to the second` MEANS
    IF firstConstructionWouldPromoteThePurposeOrObject AND (NOT secondConstructionWouldPromoteThePurposeOrObject)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE VicMatterOrDocument IS ONE OF
    VicIndicationProvidedByTheEnactmentAsPrintedByAuthorityIncludingPunctuation  -- (b)(i)
    VicReportOfProceedingsInAHouseOfParliament                                    -- (b)(ii)
    VicExplanatoryMemorandumOrOtherDocumentLaidBeforeAHouse                       -- (b)(iii)
    VicReportOfARoyalCommissionOrSimilarBody                                      -- (b)(iv)
    VicAnyOtherMatterOrDocument

-- s 35(b): consideration may be given to any matter or document that is relevant.
-- src:480 | (b) consideration may be given to any matter or document that is relevant including but not limited to—
@ref s 35(b) (src:480)
GIVEN isRelevant IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s35(b) consideration may be given to the matter or document` MEANS
    IF isRelevant THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 35(b)(i) to (iv): the matters and documents the paragraph names; the list is "including but not limited to", so any other matter or document is not covered by the list.
-- src:481 | (i) all indications provided by the Act or subordinate instrument as printed by authority, including punctuation;
-- src:482 | (ii) reports of proceedings in any House of the Parliament;
-- src:483 | (iii) explanatory memoranda or other documents laid before or otherwise presented to any House of the Parliament; and
-- src:485 | (iv) reports of Royal Commissions, Parliamentary Committees, Law Reform Commissioners and Commissions, Boards of Inquiry, Formal Reviews or other similar bodies.
@ref s 35(b)(i) and s 35(b)(ii) and s 35(b)(iii) and s 35(b)(iv) (src:481-485)
GIVEN kind IS A VicMatterOrDocument
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s35(b)(i)-(iv) the matter or document is one the paragraph names` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN VicAnyOtherMatterOrDocument THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 36 Headings, Schedules, marginal notes and footnotes`

DECLARE VicItemPrintedWithAnEnactment IS ONE OF
    VicHeadingToAChapterPartDivisionOrSubdivision                 -- s 36(1)(a)
    VicHeadingToASchedule                                         -- s 36(1)(b)
    VicHeadingToAPartDivisionOrSubdivisionOfASchedule             -- s 36(1A)
    VicScheduleItself                                             -- s 36(2)
    VicHeadingToASectionClauseRegulationRuleOrItem                -- s 36(2A)(a)
    VicHeadingToATableColumnExampleDiagramNoteOrForm              -- s 36(2A)(b)
    VicHeadingToAnOrderOfCourtOrTribunalRules                     -- s 36(2B)(a)
    VicHeadingToAPartOfSuchAnOrder                                -- s 36(2B)(b)
    VicMarginalNote                                               -- s 36(3)
    VicFootnote                                                   -- s 36(3)
    VicEndnote                                                    -- s 36(3)
    VicExampleAtTheFootOfAProvision                               -- s 36(3A)
    VicDiagram                                                    -- s 36(3A)
    VicNoteAtTheFootOfAProvision                                  -- s 36(3A)
    VicPunctuation                                                -- s 36(3B)
    VicProvisionNumber                                            -- s 36(3C)
    VicExplanatoryMemorandumOrTableOfProvisionsBeforeTheTitle     -- s 36(3D)
    VicIndexOrOtherMaterialAfterTheEndnotes                       -- s 36(3E)
    VicAnyOtherItem

-- The test that s 36(1A), (2A), (2B), (3A) and (3B) and s 36A(2) each set out: the Act is passed (or the instrument made) on or after 1 January 2001,
-- or the item is inserted into an Act passed (or instrument made) before that date by an Act passed (or instrument made) on or after that date.
-- src:495 | (a) the Act is passed, or the subordinate instrument is made, on or after 1 January 2001; or
-- src:496 | (b) the heading is inserted into an Act passed, or subordinate instrument made, before 1 January 2001 by an Act passed, or subordinate instrument made, on or after that date.
@ref s 36(1A)(a) and (b) (src:495-496)
GIVEN passedOrMadeOn IS A DATE, insertedByEnactmentPassedOrMadeOn IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s36 the Act is passed or the instrument made on or after 1 January 2001, or the item is inserted by an enactment passed or made on or after that date` MEANS
    CONSIDER insertedByEnactmentPassedOrMadeOn
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOT (passedOrMadeOn LESS THAN `s36 first day of the period in which headings, examples, notes, diagrams and punctuation form part of an Act`)
    WHEN JUST insertedOn THEN
        (NOT (passedOrMadeOn LESS THAN `s36 first day of the period in which headings, examples, notes, diagrams and punctuation form part of an Act`))
        OR (NOT (insertedOn LESS THAN `s36 first day of the period in which headings, examples, notes, diagrams and punctuation form part of an Act`))

-- s 36(1), (1A), (2), (2A), (2B), (3), (3A) to (3E): whether the item forms part of the Act or subordinate instrument.
-- Where the text makes the item form part "if" a condition holds, a failed condition is JUST FALSE; the items subsection (3) names, and the material (3D) and (3E) name, are flat negatives.
-- src:488 | (1) Headings to—
-- src:490 | (a) Chapters, Parts, Divisions or Subdivisions into which an Act or subordinate instrument is divided; or
-- src:491 | (b) Schedules to an Act or subordinate instrument—
-- src:492 | form part of the Act or subordinate instrument.
-- src:494 | (1A) Headings to Parts, Divisions or Subdivisions into which a Schedule to an Act or subordinate instrument is divided form part of the Act or subordinate instrument if—
-- src:495 | (a) the Act is passed, or the subordinate instrument is made, on or after 1 January 2001; or
-- src:496 | (b) the heading is inserted into an Act passed, or subordinate instrument made, before 1 January 2001 by an Act passed, or subordinate instrument made, on or after that date.
-- src:497 | (2) A Schedule to an Act or subordinate instrument forms part of the Act or subordinate instrument.
-- src:499 | (2A) Headings to—
-- src:500 | (a) sections, clauses, regulations, rules or items into which an Act or subordinate instrument, or a Schedule to an Act or subordinate instrument, is divided; or
-- src:501 | (b) tables, columns, examples, diagrams, notes (being notes at the foot of provisions and not marginal notes, footnotes or endnotes) or forms in an Act or subordinate instrument—
-- src:502 | form part of the Act or subordinate instrument if—
-- src:503 | (c) the Act is passed, or the subordinate instrument is made, on or after 1 January 2001; or
-- src:504 | (d) the heading is inserted into an Act passed, or subordinate instrument made, before 1 January 2001 by an Act passed, or subordinate instrument made, on or after that date.
-- src:506 | (2B) Headings to—
-- src:507 | (a) Orders into which a subordinate instrument containing rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of a court or tribunal is divided; or
-- src:508 | (b) Parts into which an Order referred to in paragraph (a) is divided—
-- src:509 | form part of the subordinate instrument if—
-- src:510 | (c) the subordinate instrument is made on or after 1 January 2001; or
-- src:511 | (d) the heading is inserted into a subordinate instrument made before 1 January 2001 by a subordinate instrument made on or after that date.
-- src:513 | (3) No marginal note, footnote or endnote in an Act or subordinate instrument and no heading to a provision of an Act or subordinate instrument (not being a heading that forms part of the Act or subordinate instrument by force of subsection (1), (1A) or (2A)) shall be taken to form part of the Act or subordinate instrument.
-- src:515 | (3A) An example (being an example at the foot of a provision under the heading "Example" or "Examples"), diagram or note (being a note at the foot of a provision and not a marginal note, footnote or endnote) in an Act or subordinate instrument forms part of the Act or subordinate instrument if—
-- src:516 | (a) the Act is passed, or the subordinate instrument is made, on or after 1 January 2001; or
-- src:517 | (b) the example, diagram or note is inserted into an Act passed, or subordinate instrument made, before 1 January 2001 by an Act passed, or subordinate instrument made, on or after that date.
-- src:519 | (3B) Punctuation in an Act or subordinate instrument forms part of the Act or subordinate instrument if—
-- src:520 | (a) the Act is passed, or the subordinate instrument is made, on or after 1 January 2001; or
-- src:521 | (b) the punctuation is inserted into an Act passed, or subordinate instrument made, before 1 January 2001 by an Act passed, or subordinate instrument made, on or after that date.
-- src:523 | (3C) A provision number in an Act or subordinate instrument (whether passed or made before, on or after 1 January 2001) forms part of the Act or subordinate instrument.
-- src:525 | (3D) An explanatory memorandum or table of provisions printed with an Act or subordinate instrument before the title of the Act or subordinate instrument does not form part of the Act or subordinate instrument.
-- src:527 | (3E) An index or other material printed with an Act or subordinate instrument after the endnotes to the Act or subordinate instrument does not form part of the Act or subordinate instrument.
@ref s 36(1) and s 36(1A) and s 36(2) and s 36(2A) and s 36(2B) and s 36(3) and s 36(3A) and s 36(3B) and s 36(3C) and s 36(3D) and s 36(3E) (src:488-527)
GIVEN item IS A VicItemPrintedWithAnEnactment, passedOrMadeOn IS A DATE, insertedByEnactmentPassedOrMadeOn IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s36 the item forms part of the Act or subordinate instrument` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN VicHeadingToAChapterPartDivisionOrSubdivision THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN VicHeadingToASchedule THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN VicScheduleItself THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN VicProvisionNumber THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN VicMarginalNote THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN VicFootnote THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN VicEndnote THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN VicExplanatoryMemorandumOrTableOfProvisionsBeforeTheTitle THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN VicIndexOrOtherMaterialAfterTheEndnotes THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN VicAnyOtherItem THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST (`s36 the Act is passed or the instrument made on or after 1 January 2001, or the item is inserted by an enactment passed or made on or after that date` passedOrMadeOn insertedByEnactmentPassedOrMadeOn)

-- s 36(4): nothing in subsection (3) prevents consideration under s 35(b) of a marginal note, footnote, endnote or heading not forming part of the Act or subordinate instrument.
-- src:529 | (4) Nothing in subsection (3) shall be construed as preventing in the interpretation of a provision of an Act or subordinate instrument, the consideration pursuant to section 35(b) of any marginal note, footnote, endnote or heading not forming part of that Act or subordinate instrument.
@ref s 36(4) (src:529)
GIVEN item IS A VicItemPrintedWithAnEnactment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s36(4) subsection (3) prevents consideration under s 35(b) of the item` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN VicMarginalNote THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN VicFootnote THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN VicEndnote THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN VicHeadingToASectionClauseRegulationRuleOrItem THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN VicHeadingToAPartDivisionOrSubdivisionOfASchedule THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN VicHeadingToATableColumnExampleDiagramNoteOrForm THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN VicHeadingToAnOrderOfCourtOrTribunalRules THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN VicHeadingToAPartOfSuchAnOrder THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 36A Examples`

-- s 36A(2): the section applies to an example of the kind in subsection (1) if the Act is passed (or the instrument made) on or after 1 January 2001, or the example is inserted by a later enactment.
-- src:536 | (2) This section applies to an example of a kind referred to in subsection (1) included in an Act or subordinate instrument if—
-- src:537 | (a) the Act is passed, or the subordinate instrument is made, on or after 1 January 2001; or
-- src:538 | (b) the example is inserted into an Act passed, or subordinate instrument made, before 1 January 2001 by an Act passed, or subordinate instrument made, on or after that date.
@ref s 36A(2) (src:536-538)
GIVEN passedOrMadeOn IS A DATE, insertedByEnactmentPassedOrMadeOn IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s36A(2) s 36A applies to the example` MEANS
    JUST (`s36 the Act is passed or the instrument made on or after 1 January 2001, or the item is inserted by an enactment passed or made on or after that date` passedOrMadeOn insertedByEnactmentPassedOrMadeOn)

-- s 36A(1): an example at the foot of a provision under the heading "Example" or "Examples" is not exhaustive and may extend, but does not limit, the meaning of the provision.
DECLARE VicEffectOfTheExampleOnTheMeaning IS ONE OF
    VicExampleIsExhaustive
    VicExampleExtendsTheMeaning
    VicExampleLimitsTheMeaning

-- src:533 | (1) If an Act or subordinate instrument includes at the foot of a provision under the heading "Example" or "Examples" an example of the operation of the provision, the example—
-- src:534 | (a) is not exhaustive; and
-- src:535 | (b) may extend, but does not limit, the meaning of the provision.
@ref s 36A(1) (src:533-535)
GIVEN effect IS A VicEffectOfTheExampleOnTheMeaning, section36AApplies IS A BOOLEAN, isAnExampleAtTheFootUnderTheHeading IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s36A(1) the example has the effect on the meaning of the provision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT section36AApplies THEN JUST FALSE
        IF NOT isAnExampleAtTheFootUnderTheHeading THEN JUST FALSE
        IF effect EQUALS VicExampleExtendsTheMeaning THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 36B Location of penalties, examples and notes`

DECLARE VicKindOfLegislativeItemCandidate IS ONE OF
    VicPenalty
    VicExample
    VicNote
    VicSomethingElse

-- s 36B(1): legislative item means a penalty, an example or a note.
-- src:542 | (1) In this section legislative item means a penalty, an example or a note.
@ref s 36B(1) (src:542)
GIVEN kind IS A VicKindOfLegislativeItemCandidate
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s36B(1) the thing is a legislative item` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN VicSomethingElse THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 36B(2): a legislative item set out in relation to a provision is taken to be at the foot of that provision, even if preceded or followed by another legislative item relating to that provision, if it would be at the foot if no other were set out.
-- src:543 | (2) A legislative item set out in an Act or subordinate instrument in relation to a provision of that Act or subordinate instrument is to be taken to be at the foot of that provision even if it is preceded or followed by another legislative item that relates to that provision if it would be at the foot of that provision if no other legislative item were set out in relation to that provision.
@ref s 36B(2) (src:543)
GIVEN isALegislativeItemSetOutInRelationToTheProvision IS A BOOLEAN, wouldBeAtTheFootIfNoOtherLegislativeItemWereSetOut IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s36B(2) the legislative item is taken to be at the foot of the provision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT isALegislativeItemSetOutInRelationToTheProvision THEN NOTHING
        IF wouldBeAtTheFootIfNoOtherLegislativeItemWereSetOut THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 36B(3): s 36B applies to a legislative item even if it was inserted by an amending enactment that provided for its insertion before or after another specified item and did not expressly place it at the foot,
-- or the amending enactment described another specified item as being at the foot of the relevant provision.
-- src:544 | (3) This section applies in relation to a legislative item even if—
-- src:545 | (a) that item was inserted by an amending Act or subordinate instrument that provided for its insertion before or after another specified legislative item and did not expressly provide for its insertion at the foot of the relevant provision; or
-- src:546 | (b) the amending Act or subordinate instrument by which it was inserted described another specified legislative item as being at the foot of the relevant provision.
@ref s 36B(3) (src:544-546)
GIVEN insertedBeforeOrAfterAnotherItemWithoutSayingAtTheFoot IS A BOOLEAN, amendingEnactmentDescribedAnotherItemAsAtTheFoot IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s36B(3) s 36B applies to the legislative item` MEANS
    IF insertedBeforeOrAfterAnotherItemWithoutSayingAtTheFoot OR amendingEnactmentDescribedAnotherItemAsAtTheFoot
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE VicPurposeForWhichS36BHasEffect IS ONE OF
    VicSection111OfTheSentencingAct1991
    VicSection36_3AOfThisAct
    VicSection36AOfThisAct
    VicAnyOtherPurpose

-- s 36B(4): without limiting its application, s 36B has effect for the purposes of s 111 of the Sentencing Act 1991 and ss 36(3A) and 36A of this Act.
-- src:547 | (4) Without limiting its application, this section has effect for the purposes of section 111 of the Sentencing Act 1991 and sections 36(3A) and 36A of this Act.
@ref s 36B(4) (src:547)
GIVEN purpose IS A VicPurposeForWhichS36BHasEffect
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s36B(4) s 36B has effect for the purpose` MEANS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN VicAnyOtherPurpose THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 37 Gender and number`

DECLARE VicFormOfWord IS ONE OF
    VicWordImportingAGender
    VicWordInTheSingular
    VicWordInThePlural

DECLARE VicWhatTheWordMayAlsoMean IS ONE OF
    VicEveryOtherGender
    VicThePlural
    VicTheSingular

-- s 37(a), (c), (d): unless the contrary intention appears, words importing a gender include every other gender, words in the singular include the plural and words in the plural include the singular.
-- src:552 | (a) words importing a gender include every other gender; and
-- src:555 | (c) words in the singular include the plural; and
-- src:556 | (d) words in the plural include the singular.
@ref s 37(a) and s 37(c) and s 37(d) (src:552-556)
GIVEN form IS A VicFormOfWord, alsoMeans IS A VicWhatTheWordMayAlsoMean, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s37 the word includes the other` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        IF form EQUALS VicWordImportingAGender AND alsoMeans EQUALS VicEveryOtherGender THEN JUST TRUE
        IF form EQUALS VicWordInTheSingular AND alsoMeans EQUALS VicThePlural THEN JUST TRUE
        IF form EQUALS VicWordInThePlural AND alsoMeans EQUALS VicTheSingular THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 38AAA References to Departments`

-- s 38AAA: if a reference is made in an Act or subordinate instrument to a particular Department, and under the Public Administration Act 2004 the name of the Department is changed, the reference is, from the date when the name is changed and so far as it relates to any period on or after that date, to be taken to be a reference to the Department by its new name.
-- src:747 | 38AAA References to Departments
-- src:748 | If—
-- src:749 | (a) reference is made in an Act or subordinate instrument to a particular Department; and
-- src:750 | (b) under the Public Administration Act 2004 the name of the Department is changed—
-- src:751 | the reference is, from the date when the name is changed and so far as it relates to any period on or after that date, to be taken to be a reference to the Department by its new name.
@ref s 38AAA (src:747-751)
GIVEN referenceIsToAParticularDepartment IS A BOOLEAN, nameChangedUnderThePublicAdministrationAct2004 IS A BOOLEAN, dayOfNameChange IS A DATE, dayOfQuestion IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s38AAA the reference is taken to be a reference to the Department by its new name for the day in question` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (referenceIsToAParticularDepartment AND nameChangedUnderThePublicAdministrationAct2004) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF dayOfQuestion LESS THAN dayOfNameChange THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 38AA References to Australian Standards, etc.`

DECLARE VicFormOfReferenceToAStandard IS ONE OF
    VicAustralianStandardOrASFollowedByANumber               -- s 38AA(1)
    VicAustralianNewZealandStandardOrASNZSFollowedByANumber  -- s 38AA(1A)
    VicAnyOtherReference

DECLARE VicPublisherOfAStandard IS ONE OF
    VicStandardsAustralia
    VicStandardsAustraliaAndTheStandardsCouncilOfNewZealandJointly
    VicNoPublisherTheTextNames

-- s 38AA(1) and (1A): the standard so numbered, published by or on behalf of Standards Australia (or jointly with the Standards Council of New Zealand).
-- src:755 | (1) In an Act or subordinate instrument, a reference consisting of the words "Australian Standard" or the letters "AS" followed in either case by a number or a number accompanied by a reference to a calendar year is a reference to the standard so numbered published by or on behalf of Standards Australia.
-- src:757 | (1A) In an Act or subordinate instrument, a reference consisting of the expression "Australian/New Zealand Standard" or "AS/NZS" followed in either case by a number or a number accompanied by a reference to a calendar year is a reference to the standard so numbered published jointly by or on behalf of Standards Australia and the Standards Council of New Zealand.
@ref s 38AA(1) and s 38AA(1A) (src:755-757)
GIVEN form IS A VicFormOfReferenceToAStandard
GIVETH A VicPublisherOfAStandard
`s38AA(1),(1A) the publisher of the standard the reference points at` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN VicAustralianStandardOrASFollowedByANumber THEN VicStandardsAustralia
    WHEN VicAustralianNewZealandStandardOrASNZSFollowedByANumber THEN VicStandardsAustraliaAndTheStandardsCouncilOfNewZealandJointly
    WHEN VicAnyOtherReference THEN VicNoPublisherTheTextNames

-- s 38AA(2): a reference to Standards Australia includes the Standards Association of Australia as constituted before 1 July 1999.
-- src:758 | (2) In an Act or subordinate instrument, a reference to Standards Australia includes a reference to the Standards Association of Australia as constituted before 1 July 1999.
@ref s 38AA(2) (src:758)
GIVEN organisationReferredTo IS A STRING, dayAsConstituted IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s38AA(2) a reference to Standards Australia includes the Standards Association of Australia as constituted on the day` MEANS
    IF organisationReferredTo EQUALS "Standards Association of Australia" AND dayAsConstituted LESS THAN `s38AA(2) day Standards Australia took over from the Standards Association of Australia`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 38AA(3): a reference to the Standards Association of Australia, so far as it relates to any period on or after 1 July 1999, is a reference to Standards Australia.
-- src:759 | (3) In an Act or subordinate instrument, a reference to the Standards Association of Australia, so far as it relates to any period on or after 1 July 1999, is a reference to Standards Australia.
@ref s 38AA(3) (src:759)
GIVEN organisationReferredTo IS A STRING, dayOfQuestion IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s38AA(3) a reference to the Standards Association of Australia is a reference to Standards Australia on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (organisationReferredTo EQUALS "Standards Association of Australia") THEN NOTHING
        IF dayOfQuestion LESS THAN `s38AA(2) day Standards Australia took over from the Standards Association of Australia` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 38EA Definition of registered medical practitioner`

-- s 38EA(2): the section applies to an Act passed, or a subordinate instrument made, on or after 1 July 2015;
-- or to an Act passed or instrument made before 1 July 2015 into which a reference to registered medical practitioner is inserted on or after that date and which did not contain such a reference immediately before that date.
-- src:822 | (2) This section applies to—
-- src:823 | (a) an Act that is passed, or a subordinate instrument that is made, on or after 1 July 2015; or
-- src:824 | (b) an Act that is passed, or a subordinate instrument that is made, before 1 July 2015—
-- src:825 | (i) into which a reference to registered medical practitioner is inserted on or after 1 July 2015; and
-- src:826 | (ii) which does not contain a reference to registered medical practitioner immediately before 1 July 2015.
@ref s 38EA(2) (src:822-826)
GIVEN passedOrMadeOn IS A DATE, referenceInsertedOn IS A MAYBE DATE, containedAReferenceImmediatelyBeforeThatDate IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s38EA(2) s 38EA applies to the Act or subordinate instrument` MEANS
    IF NOT (passedOrMadeOn LESS THAN `s38EA(2) first day on which registered medical practitioner is defined`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER referenceInsertedOn
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST insertedOn THEN
             IF (NOT (insertedOn LESS THAN `s38EA(2) first day on which registered medical practitioner is defined`)) AND (NOT containedAReferenceImmediatelyBeforeThatDate)
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 38M Satisfying print newspaper publication requirements`

DECLARE VicWayOfPublishingTheNotice IS ONE OF
    VicInAPrintNewspaperCirculatingGenerallyInVictoria
    VicOnAnApprovedAlternativePublicationInternetSite   -- s 38M(1)(a)
    VicInAPrescribedManner                              -- s 38M(1)(b)
    VicOnAPrescribedPlatform                            -- s 38M(1)(c)
    VicInSomeOtherWay

-- s 38M(1): if an Act, a statutory rule or any other subordinate instrument requires notice to be published in a print newspaper circulating generally in Victoria, the requirement is taken to have been met, for all purposes, if the notice is published on an approved alternative publication Internet site, in a prescribed manner or on a prescribed platform.
-- src:873 | (1) If an Act, a statutory rule or any other subordinate instrument requires notice (however described) to be published in a print newspaper circulating generally in Victoria that requirement is taken to have been met, for all purposes, if the notice is published—
-- src:874 | (a) on an approved alternative publication Internet site; or
-- src:875 | (b) in a prescribed manner; or
-- src:876 | (c) on a prescribed platform.
@ref s 38M(1) (src:873-876)
GIVEN requirementIsToPublishInAPrintNewspaperCirculatingGenerallyInVictoria IS A BOOLEAN, waySatisfied IS A VicWayOfPublishingTheNotice
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s38M(1) the requirement to publish in a print newspaper is taken by this subsection to have been met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT requirementIsToPublishInAPrintNewspaperCirculatingGenerallyInVictoria THEN JUST FALSE
        IF waySatisfied EQUALS VicInSomeOtherWay THEN JUST FALSE
        IF waySatisfied EQUALS VicInAPrintNewspaperCirculatingGenerallyInVictoria THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 38M(2): without limiting subsection (1), a requirement to provide a copy of a notice published in a print newspaper, or to distribute or use such a notice for any purpose, is taken to have been met by providing, distributing or using an electronic notice published in accordance with subsection (1).
-- src:877 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1), any requirement under an Act, a statutory rule or any other subordinate instrument to provide a copy of a notice published in a print newspaper or to distribute or use a notice published in a print newspaper for any purpose is taken to have been met by providing, distributing or using an electronic notice published in accordance with subsection (1).
@ref s 38M(2) (src:877)
GIVEN requirementIsToProvideDistributeOrUseACopyOfANoticePublishedInAPrintNewspaper IS A BOOLEAN, electronicNoticeWasPublishedInAccordanceWithSubsection1 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s38M(2) the requirement to provide, distribute or use a copy of the notice is taken to have been met` MEANS
    IF requirementIsToProvideDistributeOrUseACopyOfANoticePublishedInAPrintNewspaper AND electronicNoticeWasPublishedInAccordanceWithSubsection1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 38M(2A): subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to a requirement to provide for the publication of a notice published in a print newspaper in a particular locality.
-- src:878 | (2A) For the avoidance of doubt, subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to any requirement under an Act, a statutory rule or any other subordinate instrument to provide for the publication of a notice published in a print newspaper in a particular locality.
@ref s 38M(2A) (src:878)
GIVEN requirementIsToProvideForPublicationInAPrintNewspaperInAParticularLocality IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s38M(2A) subsections (1) and (2) apply to the requirement` MEANS
    IF requirementIsToProvideForPublicationInAPrintNewspaperInAParticularLocality THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 38M(3): the regulations may exempt an entity or class of entity, or a document or class of document, from the application of the section.
-- src:879 | (3) The regulations may exempt an entity or a class of entity or a document (including an Act, a statutory rule or any other subordinate instrument) or class of document from the application of this section.
@ref s 38M(3) (src:879)
GIVEN theRegulationsExemptTheEntityOrDocument IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s38M(3) s 38M applies to the entity or document` MEANS
    IF theRegulationsExemptTheEntityOrDocument THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 38M(4): nothing in the section limits the manner or form in which a notice may be published, or exempts any entity from any other obligation about publication other than in a print newspaper.
DECLARE VicThingS38MMightLimitOrExempt IS ONE OF
    VicTheMannerOrFormInWhichANoticeRequiredToBePublishedMayBePublished   -- s 38M(4)(a)
    VicAnEntityFromAnotherObligationAboutPublicationOtherThanInAPrintNewspaper   -- s 38M(4)(b)
    VicAnyOtherThingS38MMightLimit

-- src:880 | (4) Nothing in this section—
-- src:881 | (a) limits the manner or form in which any notice required to be published by an Act, a statutory rule or other subordinate instrument may be published; or
-- src:882 | (b) exempts any entity from complying with any other obligation or requirement under the Act, statutory rule or other subordinate instrument to which the notice relates in relation to the publication of the notice other than in a print newspaper.
@ref s 38M(4) (src:880-882)
GIVEN thing IS A VicThingS38MMightLimitOrExempt
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s38M(4) s 38M limits or exempts the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN VicAnyOtherThingS38MMightLimit THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 38N Minister may approve alternative publications Internet site`

-- s 38N: the Minister, by notice published in the Government Gazette, may declare one or more Internet sites to be an approved alternative publication Internet site for the purposes of s 38M.
-- src:885 | 38N Minister may approve alternative publications Internet site
-- src:886 | The Minister, by notice published in the Government Gazette, may declare one or more Internet sites to be an approved alternative publication Internet site on which publications can be made for the purposes of section 38M.
@ref s 38N (src:885-886)
GIVEN declaredByTheMinisterByNoticePublishedInTheGovernmentGazette IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s38N the Internet site is an approved alternative publication Internet site` MEANS
    IF declaredByTheMinisterByNoticePublishedInTheGovernmentGazette THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 38O Minister may make and publish guidelines`

-- s 38O(2): the guidelines must be published in the Government Gazette and on an approved alternative publication Internet site (if any), and may also be published in any other manner the Minister considers appropriate.
-- src:894 | (2) The guidelines under subsection (1)—
-- src:895 | (a) must be published in the Government Gazette and on an approved alternative publication Internet site (if any); and
-- src:896 | (b) may also be published in any other manner that the Minister considers appropriate.
@ref s 38O(2) (src:894-896)
GIVEN publishedInTheGovernmentGazette IS A BOOLEAN, anApprovedAlternativePublicationInternetSiteExists IS A BOOLEAN, publishedOnAnApprovedSite IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s38O(2)(a) the guidelines have been published as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF publishedInTheGovernmentGazette AND ((NOT anApprovedAlternativePublicationInternetSiteExists) OR publishedOnAnApprovedSite)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 38P Entities to have regard to guidelines`

-- s 38P: a Department, public statutory authority or prescribed entity responsible for the publication of a notice must have regard to the guidelines made under s 38O when publishing any notice by electronic means.
-- src:899 | 38P Entities to have regard to guidelines
-- src:900 | Any Department, public statutory authority or any prescribed entity that is responsible under an Act, a statutory rule or any other subordinate instrument for the publication of a notice (however described) must have regard to the guidelines made under section 38O when publishing any notice by electronic means.
@ref s 38P (src:899-900)
GIVEN isADepartmentPublicStatutoryAuthorityOrPrescribedEntityResponsibleForPublication IS A BOOLEAN, publishingByElectronicMeans IS A BOOLEAN, hadRegardToTheGuidelines IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s38P the entity has complied with the duty to have regard to the guidelines` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (isADepartmentPublicStatutoryAuthorityOrPrescribedEntityResponsibleForPublication AND publishingByElectronicMeans) THEN NOTHING
        IF hadRegardToTheGuidelines THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 39 Parts of speech and grammatical forms`

-- s 39: where a word or phrase is given a particular meaning in an Act or subordinate instrument, other parts of speech and grammatical forms of that word or phrase have, unless the contrary intention appears, corresponding meanings.
-- src:902 | 39 Parts of speech and grammatical forms
-- src:903 | Where a word or phrase is given a particular meaning in an Act or subordinate instrument, other parts of speech and grammatical forms of that word or phrase have, unless the contrary intention appears, corresponding meanings.
@ref s 39 (src:902-903)
GIVEN wordOrPhraseIsGivenAParticularMeaning IS A BOOLEAN, isAnotherPartOfSpeechOrGrammaticalForm IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s39 the other part of speech or grammatical form has a corresponding meaning` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (wordOrPhraseIsGivenAParticularMeaning AND isAnotherPartOfSpeechOrGrammaticalForm) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 39A Definitions inserted by amending Act or subordinate instrument`

-- s 39A: if an enactment amends a provision containing definitions by inserting another definition but does not specify where it is to be inserted, it must be taken to be inserted in the appropriate alphabetical position.
-- src:906 | 39A Definitions inserted by amending Act or subordinate instrument
-- src:907 | If an Act or subordinate instrument amends a provision of another Act or another subordinate instrument that contains definitions by inserting another definition in that provision but does not specify where in that provision the definition is to be inserted, it must be taken to be inserted in the appropriate alphabetical position.
@ref s 39A (src:906-907)
GIVEN amendsAProvisionContainingDefinitionsByInsertingAnother IS A BOOLEAN, specifiesWhereTheDefinitionIsToBeInserted IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s39A the inserted definition is taken to be inserted in the appropriate alphabetical position` MEANS
    IF amendsAProvisionContainingDefinitionsByInsertingAnother AND (NOT specifiesWhereTheDefinitionIsToBeInserted)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 39B Numbering consequential on insertion of new provisions`

DECLARE VicKindOfUndividedProvision IS ONE OF
    VicSectionNotDividedIntoSubsections        -- s 39B(1)
    VicRegulationOrRuleNotDividedIntoSubregulationsOrSubrules   -- s 39B(2)
    VicClauseOfAScheduleNotDividedIntoSubclauses                -- s 39B(3)
    VicAnyOtherKindOfProvision

-- s 39B(1) to (3), (4): where an undivided section, regulation, rule or clause is amended by inserting one or more subdivisions at the end of it, the provision as in force immediately before the amendment is taken to be subsection (1) etc. and to be amended by inserting "(1)" at its beginning.
-- Subsection (4): the section applies only to amendments made by an Act passed, or statutory rule made, on or after the commencement of the Interpretation of Legislation (Amendment) Act 1997.
-- src:911 | (1) If a section that is not divided into subsections is amended by the insertion of one or more subsections at the end of it, the section as in force immediately before the commencement of the amendment must be taken to be subsection (1) of that section and to be amended, by force of the amending provision, by the insertion of the expression "(1)" at the beginning of it.
-- src:912 | (2) If a statutory rule containing regulations or rules includes a regulation or rule that is not divided into subregulations or subrules and that regulation or rule is amended by the insertion at the end of it of one or more subregulations or subrules, the regulation or rule as in force immediately before the commencement of the amendment must be taken to be subregulation (1) of that regulation or subrule (1) of that rule (as the case requires) and to be amended, by force of the amending provision, by the insertion of the expression "(1)" at the beginning of it.
-- src:913 | (3) If a clause of a Schedule to an Act or statutory rule that is not divided into subclauses is amended by the insertion of one or more subclauses at the end of it, the clause as in force immediately before the commencement of the amendment must be taken to be subclause (1) of that clause and to be amended, by force of the amending provision, by the insertion of the expression "(1)" at the beginning of it.
-- src:914 | (4) This section applies only to amendments made by an Act passed, or statutory rule made, on or after the commencement of the Interpretation of Legislation (Amendment) Act 1997.
@ref s 39B(1) and s 39B(2) and s 39B(3) and s 39B(4) (src:911-914)
GIVEN kind IS A VicKindOfUndividedProvision, amendedByInsertingAtTheEnd IS A BOOLEAN, amendmentMadeByEnactmentPassedOrMadeOnOrAfterCommencementOfThe1997Act IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s39B the provision as in force immediately before the amendment is taken to be the first subdivision and to be amended by inserting the expression (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF kind EQUALS VicAnyOtherKindOfProvision THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT amendedByInsertingAtTheEnd THEN JUST FALSE
        IF NOT amendmentMadeByEnactmentPassedOrMadeOnOrAfterCommencementOfThe1997Act THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
